No, plurals are quite easy in Chinese. Words don't change in the plural
form (except sometimes, optionally, for people).

A bottle of water would be "yi ping shui" (one-bottle-water) and five
bottles of water would be "wu ping shui" (five-bottle-water).  No need
to change the forms of words, and no "a/an" problem.



